    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43379" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάν</span></b>  [<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ] ʽεὔἁν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.T.
					642.18
				</span></i>
			, Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.503
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.12
			</span></i>), <i>euhan</i>, a cry of the Bacchanals, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοῖ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				326
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Trag.</u>
				38
			</span></i>.—Acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, an Indian name for <i>ivy</i>, which was sacred to
			Bacchus.</div>
